From 764c99481f3210d9990c0a2f9d4ef08baadc3989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:37:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: thermal: Let the SC2 register tuple define its
 length

The binding meta-schema rejects redundant minItems when a fixed
items tuple already declares exactly two SC2 resources. Remove that
redundancy without weakening the sensor/trim resource contract.

Found by dt-doc-validate in the post-commit combined validation round.
The failing output is retained; verification resumes after this commit.

Change-Id: I03bec09b485add955e680201a096954bc11e2774
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/amlogic,thermal.yaml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/amlogic,thermal.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/amlogic,thermal.yaml
index ba5e91cdd406c05e2726e91c3b8c35cfa88f9339..47117900b411f0ab668d83384ce6f3433d3b7b83 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/amlogic,thermal.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/thermal/amlogic,thermal.yaml
@@ -69,7 +69,6 @@ allOf:
     then:
       properties:
         reg:
-          minItems: 2
           items:
             - description: Sensor registers
             - description: Calibrated trim word in the system controller
